 or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py:1-20, 29-39, 104-107, 148-158` — Preserve public exports, compatibility surface, push-state visibility, and NullHandler behavior. Consumer: public package documentation.\n- `src/rebar/_alias.py:1-12, 33-54, 154-166` — Preserve deterministic alias formats, persistence distinction, fallback, and warn-once behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_child_env.py:1-66, 103-117` — Preserve secret-name-only registry and the three environment-projection contracts. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:1-52, 87-97, 263-350, 481-495` — Preserve resolver ownership, live-read requirements, timeout posture, and repository-root selection. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:245-257, 509-515, 545-556` — Preserve current mirror omission, pandoc timeout/fallback, circuit-breaker meaning, and always-on baseline behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:1-15, 24-37, 244-276, 330-365` — Preserve file-pointer failure posture, deep layering, and active compatibility aliases/tombstones. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_config_writer.py:1-21, 222-237` — Preserve sole-writer boundary, late composition-root lookup, and atomic write behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py:1-28, 75-155, 246-249, 329-342` — Preserve permanent aliases, tombstones, registry fields, and the three current states. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_ids.py:1-41` — Preserve accepted authoring forms, deprecated four-hex warning, ambiguity handling, and path safety. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:1-19, 288-321, 393-468` — Preserve current exceptions, force shape, claim/transition/reopen semantics, and cascade behavior. Consumer: public `rebar.*` API docstrings.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_budget.py:1-15, 75-138` — Preserve actual byte budget, validated-wire sizing, and refusal-versus-truncation behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py:1-20, 141-192, 211-234` — Preserve structured error envelope, JS-safe range, recursive conversion exclusions, and registration order. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py:1-28, 88-106, 196-230, 251-341, 412-416` — Preserve thread-safe gauge, sync offload, store readiness, and instrumentation order. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py:1-31, 44-68, 137-196, 335-344` — Preserve singleflight key, private forced entries, age cleanup, and leader/follower contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:1-14, 29-97, 160-252, 261-333, 433-577` — Preserve call inputs, output shapes, polling path, read-only behavior, and failure semantics. Consumer: FastMCP tool descriptions.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:1-22, 50-59, 139-173, 274-382, 455-578` — Preserve null-versus-absence, JS-safe fields, delivery status, counted fsck fields, and tool annotations. Consumer: Pydantic/FastMCP output-schema descriptions.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_opcert_health.py:1-42, 94-97` — Preserve pinned-key comparison and serve-degraded posture. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:1-13, 173-271, 303-309, 344-465, 566-579` — Preserve status vocabularies, lean/full and bounded contracts, guide names, and errors. Consumer: FastMCP; content tests require author-guide names and the search bounded contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after 